# System Context Diagram

- **Status:** Accepted
- **Version:** 0.1
- **Repository path:** `docs/architecture/diagrams/system-context.mmd`
- **Related artifacts:** `docs/architecture/architecture-sketch.md`, `docs/architecture/component-architecture.md`, `docs/architecture/deployment-architecture.md`, `docs/api/agent-interface.md`, `docs/api/banking-api-contract.md`, `docs/api/mcp-tool-contracts.md`

## Purpose

Show the system boundary and the principal external actors or systems that interact with the Rubies MFB Customer Support Agent. This is a context-level view, not an implementation or deployment diagram.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Customer[Customer]
    Support[Human Support Staff]
    Maintainer[Project Maintainer / Evaluator]

    subgraph RubiesAgent["Rubies MFB Customer Support Agent — project boundary"]
        AgentAPI[Agent API]
        Agent[Agent Orchestration]
        Knowledge[Knowledge Base / RAG]
        Banking[Banking API]
        MCP[MCP Server]
        Session[Conversation Session Store]
        DB[(PostgreSQL — banking records and durable pending actions)]
        Vector[(Local Vector Index)]
        Model[(Versioned Local Loan Model Artifacts)]
    end

    Customer -->|Messages and confirmations| AgentAPI
    AgentAPI --> Agent
    Agent -->|Policy and product questions| Knowledge
    Knowledge --> Vector
    Agent -->|Approved tool calls| MCP
    MCP --> Banking
    Banking --> DB
    AgentAPI --> Session
    Agent -->|Eligibility assessment request| Model
    Support <-->|Escalations and handoff outcomes| Agent
    Maintainer -->|Configuration, evaluation and operations| RubiesAgent
```

## Boundary notes

- The customer interacts through the Agent API; internal banking tools are not exposed directly to the customer.
- The agent uses RAG for policy/product answers and the local vector index for retrieval.
- Agent-selected banking capabilities pass through the registered MCP tools and then the Banking API.
- PostgreSQL is the source of truth for banking records and durable pending-action state.
- Conversation session state is separate from banking persistence and is managed through the agreed Strands File Session Manager adapter. The diagram's `Conversation Session Store` box represents that adapter/storage boundary, not S3.
- The local loan model artifacts support eligibility assessment; they do not independently approve or disburse loans.
- Human support is shown as an interaction endpoint. The precise ticketing or routing integration remains undecided.
- This context diagram does not prescribe physical deployment, network topology, or final endpoint contracts.
